      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes #60871 by making mixed-attention-backend KV-cache block-size selection respect backend-specific preferred block sizes when those sizes are supported by every backend in the model.\n\nCurrently, `_preferred_block_size_for_backends()` returns the default block size (`16`) as soon as all backends support it. In multi-backend configurations, this skips `get_preferred_block_size()` entirely, even when one of the backends explicitly prefers a larger block size.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Mixed-backend models now consider each backend's preferred block size before falling back to the default.\n- A preferred size is used only when every participating backend supports it.\n- If no preferred size is common across all backends, the existing fallback logic is preserved.\n- Single-backend behavior is unchanged.\n- Added regression tests for common, incompatible, and mixed backend preferences.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded regression coverage in:\n\n`tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner.py`\n\nRelevant test command:\n\n```bash\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner.py -v",
